@startuml uc-phy-01-sequence-design
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false

title UC-PHY-01: Design Sequence Diagram – Create order, alternatives 4a, 6a and 6b

actor "Physician" as Phy
participant "client-app\n(see client diagram)" as UI
participant "OrderRestController\n(server-app)" as RC
participant "OrderServiceImpl\n(sescam-orders)" as S
participant "AccessControlService\n(C1)" as AC
participant "ExamTypeService\n(C2)" as CAT
participant "PatientSafetyGateway\n(C9 / no-op)" as SG
participant "OrderRepository\n(sescam-orders)" as R
participant "AuditService\n(C1)" as AU
participant "OrderEventPublisher\n(C5 subscribes)" as EV

== 0. Catalogue (steps 1-3) ==
Phy -> UI : order new procedure for patient
UI -> RC : GET /api/v1/orders/exam-types\n[X-Actor-Id, X-Actor-Role]
RC -> CAT : listActiveExamTypes()
CAT --> RC : List<ExamTypeDTO>
RC --> UI : 200 OK
UI --> Phy : render catalogue

== 1. Submit (steps 4-5) ==
Phy -> UI : examType, indication, justification, priority
alt 4a. Mandatory data missing [client]
  UI --> Phy : block submission, highlight fields\n(no request is sent)
else Form valid
  UI -> RC : POST /api/v1/orders\n[Body: CreateOrderPayload -> CreateOrderDTO]
  RC -> S : createOrder(request)
  S -> AC : canOrderProcedures(actorId, role)
  alt actorId blank OR not a physician
    S -> AU : recordEvent(ORDER_ACCESS_DENIED)\n[best effort, actor "UNKNOWN" if blank]
    S --> RC : throw UnauthorizedOrderAccessException (403)
  else Authorized
    S -> S : validate patientId, examTypeCode,\nindication, justification, priority
    alt Invalid (server-side 4a)
      S -> AU : recordEvent(ORDER_REJECTED) [best effort]
      S --> RC : throw InvalidOrderDataException (400)
    else Valid
      S -> CAT : getActiveExamType(examTypeCode)
      alt Unknown or inactive
        S --> RC : throw ExamTypeNotFoundException (404)
      else Found
        CAT --> S : ExamTypeDTO

        note over S, SG : <<include>> Verify Patient Safety Constraints & Contrast Allergies (step 6)
        S -> SG : getActiveConstraints(patientId)
        SG --> S : List<SafetyConstraintDTO>
        S -> S : SafetyRules.incompatibleConstraints(examType, constraints)
        alt 6b. Incompatible constraint AND overrideJustification blank
          S -> AU : recordEvent(ORDER_SAFETY_ALERT) [best effort]
          S --> RC : throw SafetyAlertException(constraints)
          RC --> UI : 422 Unprocessable [constraints]
          UI --> Phy : show contraindication alert
          alt Physician cancels
            Phy -> UI : cancel
            UI --> Phy : nothing stored
          else Physician overrides
            Phy -> UI : enter justification, resubmit
            UI -> RC : POST /api/v1/orders [same payload + overrideJustification]
            note right of S
              Same call as above: the server repeats the checks
              (stateless) and now accepts the override.
            end note
          end
        end

        note over S, EV : Persist and hand off (step 7)
        alt 6a. examType.requiresContrast OR requiresInformedConsent
          S -> S : consent = ConsentAndPreparationDTO\n(from examType: template, guide, fasting, contrast)
        end
        S -> S : build DiagnosticOrder status=PENDING_SCHEDULING,\noverrideApproved, version=1
        S -> AU : recordEvent(ORDER_CREATED | ORDER_CREATED_CONTRAST_CONSENT |\nORDER_OVERRIDE_APPROVED)
        note right of AU
          Audited before saving (NFR-11): if the audit fails,
          nothing is stored or published, so a retry
          does not create a duplicate order.
        end note
        S -> R : save(DiagnosticOrder)
        opt save fails
          S -> AU : recordEvent(ORDER_CREATION_FAILED, same order id) [best effort]
          S --> RC : storage error (500), nothing published
        end
        S -> EV : publishOrderCreated(OrderCreatedEvent)
        S --> RC : OrderResponseDTO
        RC --> UI : 201 Created [OrderResponseDTO]
        UI --> Phy : confirmation with orderNumber (step 8)
      end
    end
  end
end

note over S, EV
  Open points (module owners / team):
  1. Patient existence: PatientService.getPatientById requires canManagePatients,
     which a physician does not have. Needs a read permission or an exists() in C6.
  2. Override of an ABSOLUTE contraindication: allowed here (always justified and
     audited); confirm with clinical stakeholders.
  3. ExamTypeService is new in C2 (approval of the C2 owner).
  Audit rule: refusals (denied, rejected, safety alert) are audited best effort so a
  failing audit store never hides the 403/400/422; the audit of a stored order is
  mandatory and its failure fails the request (NFR-11).
  Client side of this flow: uc-phy-01-sequence-design-client.puml
end note
@enduml
